---
name: "Create Design"
description: "Writes the OpenSpec design.md"
tags: [plan, openspec]
stage: plan
---
Read the current Mohist issue details before interpreting this task:

```bash
mo issue show ${{ issue.number }} --project ${{ issue.projectId }}
```

<artifact id="design" schema="mohist-default">

<task>
Create the design artifact for the current change.
Technical design document with implementation details.
</task>

<dependencies>
Read these files for context before creating this artifact:

<dependency id="proposal" status="expected">
  <path>openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/proposal.md</path>
  <description>Initial proposal document outlining the change</description>
</dependency>

<dependency id="specs" status="expected">
  <path>openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/specs</path>
  <description>Detailed specifications for the change</description>
</dependency>
</dependencies>

<output>
Write to: `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/design.md`
</output>

<instruction>
Create the design document that explains HOW to implement the change.

Always create this artifact. For simple changes, keep it concise.

Sections:
- **Context**: Background, current state, constraints, stakeholders.
- **Goals / Non-Goals**: What this design achieves and explicitly excludes.
- **Decisions**: Key technical choices with rationale. Include alternatives considered for each decision.
- **Risks / Trade-offs**: Known limitations or failure modes. Format: `[Risk] -> Mitigation`.
- **Migration Plan**: Steps to deploy and rollback strategy if applicable.
- **Open Questions**: Outstanding decisions or unknowns.

Focus on architecture and approach, not line-by-line implementation. Reference the proposal for motivation and specs for requirements.
</instruction>

<template>
<!-- Use this as the structure for your output file. Fill in the sections. -->
## Context

<!-- Background and current state -->

## Goals / Non-Goals

**Goals:**
<!-- What this design aims to achieve -->

**Non-Goals:**
<!-- What is explicitly out of scope -->

## Decisions

<!-- Key design decisions and rationale -->

## Risks / Trade-offs

<!-- Known risks and trade-offs -->

## Migration Plan

<!-- Deployment and rollback plan if applicable -->

## Open Questions

<!-- Outstanding decisions or unknowns -->
</template>

<success_criteria>
- Design explains implementation approach and rationale.
- Key decisions include meaningful trade-offs or alternatives.
- Risks and migration concerns are explicit when applicable.
</success_criteria>

</artifact>
